lan review was re-signed successfully before ordinary claim. Four initial Gerrit comment/header blocks condensed; no executable/config text changed. More scoped files, independent review, recorded checks, full verify, and Gerrit remain.","timestamp":1792754120077568175},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Group10 grouped comment remediation is committed at e0d21c68207f79718c9a9f5e45508bdbf1cd69ec from fresh origin/main 91c31a4109ec34672aecac76f3ae081bf2e9a20a. Its 17 infra/gerrit paths contain 35 independently reviewed PASS comment regions. Every region is shorter; config/executable lines, directives, and shebangs are unchanged. make config-check, Terraform fmt/validate, make lint, and Gerrit-focused pytest (75 passed, 10 skipped) passed. Full untimed worktree-venv make verify is running; Gerrit push awaits the sole CI slot.","timestamp":1792761682046322597}],"created_at":1788570483492352317,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"7b2fa623-2b7a-4e34-a3a1-33599b7655c0","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"3161-93b1-f3eb-4547"},{"link_uuid":"a403c7a0-20d1-48ce-b740-f26ae8106e63","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"ae7b-84ea-41d8-4a9f"},{"link_uuid":"0dcc155e-835b-4bfc-ae86-e95cfaf5a976","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"0d0b-dcf4-105d-41cc"},{"link_uuid":"eb09042b-f2ca-4f5b-aaba-1535b2df38eb","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"20e9-7e2a-c2e6-41a2"},{"link_uuid":"4a8c63a0-55e6-4fc2-88ae-541c8318a2b1","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"85f3-d556-bd17-40cd"},{"link_uuid":"75c0684b-3d9c-4283-b86a-851e53a07e3a","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"8d8a-27d4-8603-4c8a"},{"link_uuid":"b088277f-6ed8-4062-b186-d979d1913a76","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"41c0-8644-c7b7-4703"},{"link_uuid":"8205cd09-d7c6-47bb-89f1-e4641ff9d6cf","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"b0c6-4020-68b3-4fa1"},{"link_uuid":"2ad59a19-be36-471b-a16b-c9f40bd5b11e","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"4bcc-2d8d-d72f-4289"},{"link_uuid":"13311011-d579-4e6c-9964-c0132e4d1155","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"a58b-a1f1-5d11-4b48"},{"link_uuid":"d759c757-7330-4537-bd66-a41c7fa25b2e","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"1d24-4047-d959-48aa"},{"link_uuid":"0b07e0b9-74ec-4333-bc05-a9c81c1c1d57","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"b943-19c6-a332-4228"},{"link_uuid":"aed84709-8bbf-42a3-bf84-055afa85e44a","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"acb1-2c9f-37f2-412a"},{"link_uuid":"7ee7190d-7c48-4246-b4b7-823dc6f138fd","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"5cd3-58c3-1bb0-4f99"},{"link_uuid":"44c399c0-6e38-4712-9125-72a04b165dcb","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"f50b-e579-03de-4a47"},{"link_uuid":"8204be79-c3bd-4769-aafb-81c740718a18","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"01b6-811f-05e2-4bcd"},{"link_uuid":"31385fd2-a7e4-4b50-a41f-c5396f86dd0b","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"d4b4-3d94-ca0d-4b4a"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe 17 `infra/gerrit` files below contain repeated, obvious, historical, or stale prose identified by the comment audit and revalidated on `origin/main` at `c019920390926d543a0813d4c0c8721543d98776`. Shortening it must preserve the live Gerrit security and delivery model.\n\n## Approach\nEdit only standalone comments and blank lines in the declared files. Preserve executable/configuration text byte-for-byte. Replace narration with the minimum current rationale needed by each consumer; describe known behavior gaps truthfully rather than strengthening claims.\n\n## Scope\n- `feature-branch-e2e-scenarios.sh` — Preserve sourced-driver API, `EVIDENCE:` schema, actual scenario assertions, and optional ACL probes. State accurately that scenario 4 records but does not assert Verified rerun and scenario 7 cites concurrency/backfill evidence only.\n- `feature-branch-e2e.sh` — Preserve live/manual destructive scope, credential-helper auth without password URLs, exit meanings, mirror-ref wait before CI dispatch, DCO hook, sourced scenarios, and cleanup. Do not claim cleanup reverts content already merged to main.\n- `feature-branch-inventory.sh` — Preserve 14-day default, ancestor-of-main classification, read-only default, explicit confirmed deletion on Gerrit and GitHub, and credential-helper inputs.\n- `gerrit_to_platform.ini.template` — Preserve single-placeholder rendering, 0600 output, adjacent `replication.config`, `recheck -> verify`, branch-agnostic dispatch, and pre-existing mirror branch requirement. Remove the stale claim that current CI workflows run on `feature/**`.\n- `install-plugins.sh` — Preserve two plugin identities, checksum-pinned provenance, manifest/on-disk names, cross-platform hashing, checksum idempotence, bounded download, atomic move, and OAuth-before-boot/restart requirement.\n- `materialize-deploy-key.sh` — Preserve root/instance-role execution, exact SSM parameter, empty-value failure, UID/GID 1000, restrictive modes, secret nonlogging, deduplicated `known_hosts`, container paths, and strict host checking.\n- `materialize-g2p-config.sh` — Preserve fail-closed SSM PAT handling, UID/GID/modes, safe shell substitution, copied cross-namespace replication config, stale-link removal, and missing-config warning. Do not claim direct destination writes are atomic.\n- `project.config` — Preserve DCO; contributor/admin Submit rules; proposal, feature-driver, and service-user ACLs; active LLM-Review and Verified requirements; disabled inherited Code-Review; exact vote-copy asymmetry; and Rebase-If-Necessary with `mergeContent=true`. Never describe LLM-Review as the sole gate.\n- `register-deploy-key.sh` — Preserve operator-only GitHub mutation, public-key inputs, write-enabled key, dry-run, and title-based idempotence. Keep alternative designs out of inline comments.\n- `replication.config` — Preserve site placement, project scope, explicit non-force main/tag/feature refspecs and deliberately force-scoped refs/changes/* replication, `mirror=false`, permission/meta secrecy, finite retry/timeout, persisted queue, auto-reload, and deploy-key consumer.\n- `reviewbot-e2e.sh` — Preserve live test-branch mutation, three exits, SSM secrecy, temporary replication refspec, cleanup, integer LLM-vote check, GitHub poll, and opportunistic mirror-lock probe. Do not claim it proves the full current two-vote pipeline; follow-up bug `educated-greasy-smelts` owns that behavior gap.\n- `service-user.sh` — Preserve admin-SSH creation, exact existing-account detection, delete/recreate token rotation, SSM overwrite, argument quoting, and surgical `webhooks.config` update. Describe OAuth and header-based `X-Rebar-Token`, not obsolete query-token delivery.\n- `setup-ci-service-account.sh` — Preserve admin-SSH provisioning, public-key validation/private-key rejection, SSH-only identity, Service Users membership, duplicate-key idempotence, and operator-owned private-key delivery. Describe deployed OAuth accurately.\n- `setup-project.sh` — Preserve declarative config replacement, project/group creation, additive membership, explicit removal, live UUID/name mapping including Registered Users, dry-run diff, and server-level whole-topic exclusion.\n- `setup-replication.sh` — Preserve deploy-key-first failure, site copy/mode/ownership, dry-run, opt-in reload versus default restart, kill switch, and add-new-before-remove-old rotation.\n- `smoke-check.sh` — Preserve REST and HTTPS-clone bot-token checks, trailing-slash events endpoint, SSM secrecy, accumulated result, and temporary-clone cleanup.\n- `webhooks.config` — Preserve committed secret-free template, refs/meta/config source, internal URL, `X-Rebar-Token`, patchset/comment events, retries, and rerender requirement; the secret is not URL-embedded.\n\nConsumers are Gerrit/plugins, gerrit-to-platform, deployment scripts, runbooks, CI workflows, and operators named by each file.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The leaf commit changes only standalone comments or blank lines in the 17 declared files.\n- [ ] Every Scope constraint and consumer contract has a PASS row with concrete before/after citations in a leaf-linked session log authored by a reviewer who did not write the remediation.\n- [ ] Every edited comment block has an independent `bloat-removal` PASS row confirming that redundant, obvious, duplicated, historical, or stale prose was removed while current non-obvious rationale remained.\n- [ ] Focused Gerrit/config tests, path-scoped `git diff --check`, and repository lint pass at the leaf commit.\n- [ ] No missing or FAIL semantic-preservation row remains at closure.\n\n## Verification\nRun the recorded comment-only guard, config/shell validation, focused Gerrit tests, path-scoped diff check, and worktree-venv lint. Live E2E claims are not strengthened without an executable oracle.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/gerrit/feature-branch-e2e-scenarios.sh","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"infra/gerrit/feature-branch-e2e.sh","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"infra/gerrit/feature-branch-inventory.sh","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"infra/gerrit/gerrit_to_platform.ini.template","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"infra/gerrit/install-plugins.sh","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"infra/gerrit/materialize-deploy-key.sh","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"infra/gerrit/materialize-g2p-config.sh","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"infra/gerrit/project.config","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"infra/gerrit/register-deploy-key.sh","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"infra/gerrit/replicatio